{"id": 44, "ts": 1783924743.7982705, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the panel\u2019s shift toward Candidate\u202fB based on his stress\u2011handling and conscientiousness, but the new reliability data for Candidate\u202fA changes my view. The notes confirm that A is \u201cknown to be\u202f100\u202f% reliable,\u201d and he \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d which directly addresses two critical safety criteria: operational reliability and crew cooperation. While we still lack concrete evidence of his attention to numerical data and his sense of responsibility, his proven decision\u2011quality (\u201cmakes correct decisions quickly\u201d) and calmness in crises give him a clear edge on decision quality and stress resilience\u2014areas where B has no documented examples. The concerns about A\u2019s egocentric reputation and limited willingness to further his education remain, yet these are potentially mitigable through training, whereas B\u2019s weak memory for numbers and nasty remarks pose immediate safety risks. Therefore, I now recommend **Candidate\u202fA** as the best overall fit."}
